<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jeanne Mance</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1606">1606</a>–<a href="/years/1673">1673</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jeanne Mance was a French nurse and settler who co-founded Ville-Marie, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-de-chomedey-de-maisonneuve">Paul de Chomedey de Maisonneuve</a> in 1642. She founded and ran the Hôtel-Dieu de Montréal, the city's first hospital, and helped to secure the funds and settlers that saved the struggling colony. She is honoured as a co-founder of Montreal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jeanne-mance.jpg" alt="Jeanne Mance" width="320" height="512" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sculpture : Louis-Philippe Hébert / Photo : Jeangagnon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JeanneManceHotelDieu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
